From 1dd95e40259c91b5ff395f43cd10817a74103f75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:35:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip: apu-expert-gtt P1.1 + P2 + P3a/P3b -- a mlocked GTT
 expert store, and the tier as a serving ARENA
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A UMA-only resident expert tier: ONE anonymous region (mmap + MADV_HUGEPAGE), registered ONCE
with cudaHostRegister(Mapped|ReadOnly) and mlocked, that the hottest MoE expert tables are placed
in (P2) or that serves as the expert cache's ARENA (P3) and that MUL_MAT_ID reads in place -- with
no host pool and no slab arena below it.

- the region + first-fit allocator + census live in ggml/src/ggml-cuda/gtt-expert-store.{cu,cuh};
  the buffer type is in ggml-cuda.cu on the KV-region pattern (a DEVICE buft with the plain device
  type's vtable contract and a per-device unique name), and device hooks let the model loader open
  it, ask what it may lock, and print its census.
- -lme sizes it (P1.1): N GiB exactly, or auto = MOE_HOST_LIMIT_FRAC of MemAvailable, capped at
  the set and at RLIMIT_MEMLOCK; the SAME budget and the SAME heat ranking as the discrete arm,
  decided before any tensor is placed.  It engages without -ncmoe, and common/arg.cpp gains the
  UMA branch of the help text.
- P2 (a set that FITS the store): whole expert tables are placed in it and read in place.  The
  fill is the buffered pread arm, straight from the GGUF into the slot.
- P3 (a set that does NOT fit, MOE_EXPERT_GTT_ARENA=1, opt-in): the store becomes the cache's
  arena -- try_arena() is its third slot source beside the slab and cudaMalloc -- the expert
  tensors become HOLES in the read-only model mapping (nothing allocated, nothing pinned), and the
  delivery's existing LFRU residency serves every read.  g_cold_uva is false for the tier by
  construction (an APU's cold source would be a pageable page the GPU cannot address), so every
  miss evicts and fills.  The tier forces a MAPPED load: an iGPU reports no mmap_support, and a
  copied master would be a pageable full copy of the expert set.
- mlock is what makes it a RESERVATION: probe 16 (MEASUREMENTS.md §15) measured that a
  registered-only region is RECLAIMABLE under pressure -- the kernel splits its huge pages, swaps
  0-436 MiB per 2 GiB out, the next GPU read stalls a one-off 12-37x, and Unevictable reports 0
  throughout.  So: mlock by default (MOE_EXPERT_GTT_MLOCK=0 is the kill switch), the extent
  clamped to RLIMIT_MEMLOCK, a DECLINE with the fix when the model fits in RAM anyway, and a
  REFUSAL with the shortfall when the model cannot run without the store and it cannot be locked
  (0.76 s on a 123 GiB model instead of the 2026-10-19 over-commit).  mlock is free at creation.
- MOE_EXPERT_GTT=0 (kill switch) reproduces today's behaviour and log byte for byte;
  MOE_EXPERT_GTT_RO=0 registers the region writable, the A/B that proves the read-rate claim.
- The ARENA tier is opt-in and stays opt-in until it has been measured on more than this box: no
  streaming/pipelined fill (P4), no prefill streaming (P5), no nextn pinning (P3c).  Without
  MOE_EXPERT_GTT_ARENA the run is the whole-tensor placement of P2, and the census says so.

Verified on halo (gfx1151, 123 GiB, ROCm 10.1.0): same-seed greedy text identical on 35B-A3B
(627b2ebd7792) and Flash-Next (f586785d7183) for store-off / auto / -lme 6 / the arena tier at
-lme 4, 6 and 8, and a 3x residency change on the 122B-A10B gives identical text; -lme 6 realises
exactly 6144.0 MiB; auto on a fitting set is the whole set with zero evictions; registration
26 ms/GiB; pp512 within noise of the plain device buffer for the registered READ-ONLY arm; the
lock policy's four arms pass under ulimit -l 8192; the arena tier registers all 120/144 tables,
evicts under a partial budget with 0 arena releases, and a 123.45 GiB model runs to completion at
-lme 20 and -lme 60; check-gpu-faults.sh clean.
